    "english":  "I saw it, O lord of the river-plains! I saw it with my own eyes,\nand what could I do but grieve?\nAlong the festive street where the bard\u0027s small, melodious lute\nhums sweetly like a swarm of bees in the fresh season,\nthe jeweled courtesans welcomed your return, their hearts fluttering with desire!\nAnd when the hot tears of sorrow fell from their longing eyes\nin that agonizing moment when you turned your chariot awayΓÇö\nthey looked like shipwrecked merchants clinging in terror to a single plank,\ntossed upon the surging waves, pulling and grasping in despair\nas the dark waters overwhelmed their strength!",
